XQuartz bundle: a game, for macOS Game Mode

Every X11 window of SteamARM -- a game's too -- belongs to SteamARM-X11.app,
and the bundle said public.app-category.utilities: macOS never turned Game
Mode on for it (Game Mode follows the frontmost app's games category, or
LSSupportsGameMode, when that app is in full screen). Games category,
LSSupportsGameMode and GCSupportsGameMode (controllers at the doubled
Bluetooth polling rate Game Mode gives).

--- a/hw/xquartz/bundle/Info.plist.cpp
+++ b/hw/xquartz/bundle/Info.plist.cpp
@@ -62,7 +62,11 @@
                 <string>XQUARTZ_SPARKLE_FEED_URL</string>
 #endif
 	<key>LSApplicationCategoryType</key>
-		<string>public.app-category.utilities</string>
+		<string>public.app-category.games</string>
+	<key>LSSupportsGameMode</key>
+		<true/>
+	<key>GCSupportsGameMode</key>
+		<true/>
 	<key>NSHumanReadableCopyright</key>
 		<string>© 2003-2026 Apple Inc.
 © 2003 XFree86 Project, Inc.
